  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Role and Standing
    
    Lianhingme hi'Shard is an Aurora Stack merchant of the E'frostlings — the faction that clawed its way back to prominence through the Faction Wars — and the principal organizer of Circle Gatherings at the Still Pools, the geothermally heated lagoon at the Berg's far edge. The canonical summary states she orchestrates these gatherings "with the precision of someone who has learned that coordination prevents collapse." This is accurate. Her work is logistical, not ceremonial: she arranges, checks, rearranges. Her hands do not stop moving.
    
    She carries negotiation documents in a sealed aurora-glass case slung over her left shoulder, wears a merchant's coat of white wool and silver thread whose hem is perpetually salt-stained from the Pools' spray, and bears burn scars on both flippers. The left moves slower than the right. She has not explained this.
    
    ## The Two Gatherings
    
    Two Circle Gatherings define her public record.
    
    The first brought the Midnight Claws, the Nightfall Shelf's dominant enforcement faction, and the E'frostlings together at the Still Pools to witness the ☽'micseleia' Dagger, a damaged artifact of contested provenance. Sources agree this gathering cost Lianhingme something significant. None specify what.
    
    The second concerned custody of the Radiant Ring — a corrupted aurora-glass hammer-weapon carried by the defender Netemia through multiple engagements against orca war-pods before Netemia's death. Lianhingme presented Stack lineage charts, forge-signatures, and a list of three dozen families who lost someone where the Ring was present. She called it "her people's dead god's weapon" and argued for its return to the surface. When a Luminary elder conceded the Ring instead to the Nightshelf memorial alcove Echo∴eliquiae, Lianhingme recorded the decision with her slow left flipper and let the Accord hold. The restraint in that moment deserves more attention than it has received.
    
    ## Personal Details
    
    Lianhingme was created — the records use that word, meaning shaped by circumstance — during the Orca Incursion. She mastered Slide Prism, the aurora-light harvesting technique, and The Shell Hatch not from ambition but because the ice was showing her orca movements she could not ignore. She refuses to enter the deep tunnels. She tracks exits when crowds gather. She has not been observed sleeping during festival season.
    
    She sets out three cups of fire-tea each morning. Only two are ever used.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771587515444_0", anchor: "principal organizer of Circle Gatherings at the Still Pools", text: "The Still Pools was founded on rejection of exactly this. No census, no maps, no contact with either colony. An E'frostlings merchant organizing inter-factional gatherings there is not \"coordination\" — it is the death of an isolationist settlement's founding principle. The dissidents either consented or were too few left to refuse. The entry treats both possibilities as invisible.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771587515444_1", anchor: "her people's dead god's weapon", text: "The dead god belongs to orca theology. No Aurora tradition claims one. Either the transcription is garbled, or Lianhingme borrowed orca language deliberately — describing what the Ring did to Netemia in terms taken from the enemy's faith. If deliberate, it is the sharpest theological statement in the Circle Gathering archive. If error, it needs correcting before print. I cannot determine which, and this is precisely the kind of ambiguity that must not be left to the reader's comfortable assumption.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771587515444_2", anchor: "the ice was showing her orca movements she could not ignore", text: "She mastered the technique that provoked the raids, and the ice showed her what followed. Harvesting platforms sat directly on orca feeding grounds. What she \"could not ignore\" may have included more than their aggression.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
